Maya Singh: opened PR to refresh function-calling examples and fix two schema anchors: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4999 :wave:
Owen Reed: Thanks — which anchors are broken? I hit a 404 on /schema-toolcall.md#examples yesterday.
Maya Singh: We split schema-toolcall into schema-toolcall.md and schema-types.md. PR updates links in guides/function-calling.md and samples/js-toolcall.md. Also swapping main examples to explicit "action"+"args" for clarity.
Felix Grant: Good call. Can we avoid pasting the full JSONSchema inline? Suggest minimal inline example and a collapsible link to the canonical schema. Example to show:

{"action": "summarize", "args": {"max_len": 120}}

and then an Advanced box with compact envelope: {"type":"toolcall","payload":{...}}
Owen Reed: Also add a small parser fallback snippet. Prefer balanced-brace extractor over greedy regex. Tiny python helper is fine, e.g.:

# find first balanced {} region
def first_json(s):
    depth=0; start=None
    for i,c in enumerate(s):
        if c=='{':
            if depth==0: start=i
            depth+=1
        elif c=='}':
            depth-=1
            if depth==0 and start is not None:
                return s[start:i+1]
    return None

try:
    data = json.loads(resp)
except ValueError:
    candidate = first_json(resp)
    data = json.loads(candidate) if candidate else None

Maya Singh: Perfect. I'll add that and a tiny JS equivalent. Also fixed the two anchors and updated the PR description to call out the checklist for docs authors (use explicit action/args, link to schema, include fallback section if needed).
